{"term":"كوس","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"kūs","category":"organs","subcategory":"vagina","concept":"vagina","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":95,"technical":2,"recognition_pct_current":85,"recognition_pct_peak":85,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Dialectal phonological variant of كس; crude slang for the vagina with the same vulgar force as the base form, widely used in Egyptian, Levantine, and Mesopotamian Arabic.","english_term":"cunt","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Near-synonym of كس differing only in vowel pattern; carries essentially identical crude register; more common in Egyptian and Levantine varieties than in Gulf Arabic."}
{"term":"حفرة","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"ḥufra","category":"organs","subcategory":"vagina","concept":"vagina","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":70,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":75,"recognition_pct_peak":75,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Crude slang for the vagina literally meaning 'hole' or 'pit'; dehumanizes by reducing female genitalia to a penetrable cavity.","english_term":"hole","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The 'hole' metaphor for vagina is cross-linguistically common; crude through reductionism rather than phonetic taboo; primary literal meaning is excavation pit or ditch."}
