{"term":"شقّة","lang":"ar","script":"arab","romanization":"shaqqa","category":"organs","subcategory":"vagina","concept":"vagina","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":72,"technical":3,"recognition_pct_current":70,"recognition_pct_peak":70,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Crude slang for the vagina based on the meaning 'crack' or 'split'; references the visible labial cleft as the defining feature.","english_term":"slit","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Shares orthography with the modern colloquial Arabic word for 'apartment' (شقة, from the same root شق meaning to split apart); dual meaning enables crude wordplay in everyday speech."}
